WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.603
The narrator of Bridgerton
is Julie Andrews.

00:00:03.603 --> 00:00:05.420
The great Julie Andrews.
Yes.

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:10.420
And I know, I mean, the word
icon doesn't even do justice

00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:13.860
to who Julie Andrews is,

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:15.800
and what she's accomplished.
I know.

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:17.290
Because she's the narrator of the show,

00:00:17.290 --> 00:00:19.632
have you had a chance to meet her?

00:00:19.632 --> 00:00:21.280
I haven't, I haven't.

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:24.813
And it's haunted me ever
since the pandemic started.

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:29.810
I actually read her
autobiography in lockdown,

00:00:29.810 --> 00:00:32.406
because I just wanted to be close to her.

00:00:32.406 --> 00:00:34.840
I was so disappointed
we didn't get to meet,

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:37.330
so I just found out everything I could

00:00:37.330 --> 00:00:38.820
about Julie Andrews so that now

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:41.230
I feel like I know her.

00:00:41.230 --> 00:00:42.460
And if we ever meet in person

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:44.190
I have something to talk to her about.

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:46.220
Although I worry that
might scare her away.

00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:48.660
So I might play it a bit cooler.

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:50.620
Yeah, sometimes that frightens people,

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:51.910
when you say--
Yeah.

00:00:51.910 --> 00:00:55.670
When you say, 'oh, you know,
Phoebe meet Julie Andrews.'

00:00:55.670 --> 00:01:00.640
'You were born in Leeds in
1928, you weigh 135 grams.'

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:01.473
You know, you don't want to say

00:01:01.473 --> 00:01:02.940
that kind of stuff to people,

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:04.123
it sounds creepy.

00:01:05.014 --> 00:01:05.847
No.

00:01:05.847 --> 00:01:08.873
I have to tell you, I've
been very fortunate,

00:01:09.934 --> 00:01:11.740
over a long career, I've been able to meet

00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:13.100
just about everybody.

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:15.230
Never had the chance
to meet Julie Andrews.

00:01:15.230 --> 00:01:16.880
But they have something
here in the States,

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:18.050
the Macy's Day Parade,

00:01:18.050 --> 00:01:19.880
which is a big deal on Thanksgiving.

00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:21.523
And I was in New York once,

00:01:21.523 --> 00:01:23.850
just before I left about 10 years ago.

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:26.180
And the Macy's Day Parade was going by,

00:01:26.180 --> 00:01:27.770
and I was holding my daughter,

00:01:27.770 --> 00:01:29.583
who was just a baby at the time.

00:01:29.583 --> 00:01:32.370
And suddenly right in front of me,

00:01:32.370 --> 00:01:36.100
Julie Andrews goes by on top
of the parade float waving.

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:38.090
I dropped daughter practically,

00:01:38.090 --> 00:01:41.507
and started screaming,
"Julie Andrews, Julie."

00:01:42.432 --> 00:01:46.120
And I think she saw, I don't
think she recognized me.

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:48.627
But she thought, who's that
horrible woman (laughs).

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:53.600
I completely lost it, that's
the effect she has on people.

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:55.561
She does, yeah, she does.

00:01:55.561 --> 00:01:58.073
She's basically a royal.

